$ |\n| $9$ | $27$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186455473 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073894 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b9357cc9-e383-5d88-9741-f49f6fbcca99" :knowledge-point/title "Filling a Ratio Table by Multiplying: Missing Denominators"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4cc138c2-e90d-5f57-8ac1-8287ccae8fb6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186455034} {:answer/id #uuid "9f632e95-bd21-56d4-9e71-5831e2f4bc12" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186455188} {:answer/id #uuid "d6760e45-5734-5f89-b9db-02339be9fc03" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186455278} {:answer/id #uuid "f55bf677-d168-5bf0-81b6-605b613ed5cb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186455323} {:answer/id #uuid "fa1fca0d-5971-54b5-9a02-2164a0393773" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186455334}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fa1fca0d-5971-54b5-9a02-2164a0393773" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186455334} :answer-field/id #uuid "c9f67718-c30c-53ea-8c6b-740f8fbb79d1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186455410}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8252affb-ce2c-5680-9903-2378ac435a36" :question/math-academy-id "q-59908" :question/problem "| $4$ | $8$ |\n| --- | --- |\n| $12$ | $?$ |\n| $20$ | $40$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nWhat number is missing from the ratio table?" :question/worked-solution "We start with the ratio $4:8$ and write it as a fraction:\n\n$$\n\\frac{4}{8}\n$$\n\nSo the numerator represents the left-hand entry ($4$), and the denominator represents the right-hand entry ($8$).\n\nWe can make a numerator of $12$ by multiplying the numerator and denominator by $3$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4\\times 3}{8\\times 3} & =\\frac{12}{24}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe add this to our ratio table:\n\n| $4$ | $8$ |\n| --- | --- |\n| $12$ | $24$ |\n| $20$ | $40$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nSo, the missing number is $24.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186455501 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073895 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6e3287b0-2ecb-5d83-9596-7943d68f8884" :knowledge-point/title "Filling a Ratio Table by Multiplying: Missing Numerators"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "14da0cce-51ba-52e3-9233-86746af85c62" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$25$ and $18$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454940} {:answer/id #uuid "1f57a605-82c6-5051-a1ba-842a49b1b335" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$20$ and $18$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454952} {:answer/id #uuid "28cb5c80-343b-58d3-9289-912d69ccd568" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$15$ and $15$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454966} {:answer/id #uuid "575dcf24-6e16-5de7-b066-f37a2862ab06" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$20$ and $21$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186455055} {:answer/id #uuid "67a009a7-38a6-5f01-bf7a-e64f34a5eca5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$10$ and $15$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186455093}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1f57a605-82c6-5051-a1ba-842a49b1b335" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$20$ and $18$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454952} :answer-field/id #uuid "f3474f11-af66-5518-b854-1cdd4039db31" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186455426}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "dbd602d5-dd56-5f28-af09-18b7c946837e" :question/math-academy-id "q-59919" :question/problem "From top to bottom, what are the missing numbers in the ratio table below?\n\n| $3$ | $5$ |\n| --- | --- |\n| $12$ | $?$ |\n| $?$ | $30$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We start with the ratio $3:5$ and write it as a fraction:\n\n$$\n\\frac{3}{5}\n$$\n\nSo the numerator represents the left-hand entry ($3$), and the denominator represents the right-hand entry ($5$).\n\nWe can generate equivalent ratios by finding equivalent fractions:\n\n- To create a numerator of $12,$ we multiply the numerator and denominator of our fraction by $4:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{3\\times 4}{5\\times 4}=\\frac{12}{20}\n$$\n\n- To create a denominator of $30,$ we multiply the numerator and denominator of our fraction by $6:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{3\\times 6}{5\\times 6}=\\frac{18}{30}\n$$\n\nFinally, we fill in the ratio table:\n\n| $3$ | $5$ |\n| --- | --- |\n| $12$ | $20$ |\n| $18$ | $30$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nSo, from top to bottom, the missing numbers are $20$ and $18.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186455446 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073895 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6e3287b0-2ecb-5d83-9596-7943d68f8884" :knowledge-point/title "Filling a Ratio Table by Multiplying: Missing Numerators"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4d10cdf4-6781-5eff-ace5-24389d9da09a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$20$ and $36$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186455035} {:answer/id #uuid "610b5d00-47bf-5fde-81d4-cf9e5c20321f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$25$ and $30$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186455078} {:answer/id #uuid "79748308-7ed9-59fa-b641-d77c77cce124" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$15$ and $18$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186455126} {:answer/id #uuid "9897e9a7-c28a-5174-ae10-b4cc814cf434" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$25$ and $36$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186455181} {:answer/id #uuid "b15ca865-115b-5ec5-b682-8e85963271a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$20$ and $30$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186455213}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4d10cdf4-6781-5eff-ace5-24389d9da09a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$20$ and $36$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186455035} :answer-field/id #uuid "ad0791ec-ba86-59af-80db-e0d45756c328" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186455398}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "40bbff9d-d33b-5344-bec9-19d7e575474d" :question/math-academy-id "q-59921" :question/problem "From top to bottom, what are the missing numbers in the ratio table below?\n\n| $5$ | $6$ |\n| --- | --- |\n| $?$ | $24$ |\n| $30$ | $?$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We start with the ratio $5:6$ and write it as a fraction:\n\n$$\n\\frac{5}{6}\n$$\n\nSo the numerator represents the left-hand entry ($5$), and the denominator represents the right-hand entry ($6$).\n\nWe can generate equivalent ratios by finding equivalent fractions:\n\n- To create a denominator of $24,$ we multiply the numerator and denominator of our fraction by $4:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{5\\times 4}{6\\times 4}=\\frac{20}{24}\n$$\n\n- To create a numerator of $30,$ we multiply the numerator and denominator of our fraction by $6:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{5\\times 6}{6\\times 6}=\\frac{30}{36}\n$$\n\nFinally, we fill in the ratio table:\n\n| $5$ | $6$ |\n| --- | --- |\n| $20$ | $24$ |\n| $30$ | $36$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nSo, from top to bottom, the missing numbers are $20$ and $36.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186455465 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073896 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "60021495-9d2a-58a5-9321-bb16013bbba7" :knowledge-point/title "Filling a Ratio Table by Multiplying and Dividing"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "03982a3d-b698-5cbc-9d2a-69e4fb2d8065" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$3$ and $12$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454910} {:answer/id #uuid "6bba0edd-993f-54e4-a048-824d34e1cd48" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$12$ and $8$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186455104} {:answer/id #uuid "a01c7926-bbc0-5c2b-a7a7-1e039a2f7cda" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$1$ and $60$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186455190} {:answer/id #uuid "e2e1e419-a2ab-533d-8a4a-11d178051877" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$8$ and $4$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186455295} {:answer/id #uuid "ebaceeee-c9cb-58a1-a200-48e7ba2095ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$8$ and $6$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186455313}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e2e1e419-a2ab-533d-8a4a-11d178051877" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$8$ and $4$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186455295} :answer-field/id #uuid "9cc223b1-a51e-5700-b7e2-be0125a1cd8b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186455392}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "6997b2fa-6238-5241-b0d8-8e5218a5b865" :question/math-academy-id "q-59926" :question/problem "From top to bottom, what are the missing numbers in the ratio table below?\n\n| $2$ | $?$ |\n| --- | --- |\n| $?$ | $16$ |\n| $6$ | $24$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We start with the ratio $6:24$ and write it as a fraction:\n\n$$\n\\frac{6}{24}\n$$\n\nSo the numerator represents the left-hand entry ($6$), and the denominator represents the right-hand entry ($24$).\n\nWe can generate equivalent ratios by finding equivalent fractions:\n\n- To create a numerator of $2,$ we divide the numerator and denominator of our fraction by $3:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{6÷3}{24÷3}=\\frac{2}{8}\n$$\n\n- To create a denominator of $16,$ we multiply the numerator and denominator of the previous fraction by $2:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{2\\times 2}{8\\times 2}=\\frac{4}{16}\n$$\n\nFinally, we fill in the ratio table:\n\n| $2$ | $8$ |\n| --- | --- |\n| $4$ | $16$ |\n| $6$ | $24$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nSo, from top to bottom, the missing numbers are $8$ and $4.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186455502 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186073897 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "84a526bf-9d98-54e1-a54e-cd625bbaea49" :knowledge-point/title "Word Problems"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "45b1dd72-a280-5786-9c0c-78bfc1059520" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$7$ liters" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186455019} {:answer/id #uuid "52d99b57-1f93-5ce2-8fa0-0b81d4a6db9e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$4$ liters" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186455051} {:answer/id #uuid "b515f4a3-f4c9-5b94-bfca-1a1cd1c43525" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$6$ liters" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186455220} {:answer/id #uuid "ba74b686-4983-5947-8325-76e2a9877067" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$8$ liters" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186455228} {:answer/id #uuid "f5e2586b-5055-5e6a-8fd8-2cfa7a0648a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$5$ liters" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186455324}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f5e2586b-5055-5e6a-8fd8-2cfa7a0648a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$5$ liters" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186455324} :answer-field/id #uuid "85127a9c-4be9-56e7-b690-1f020f8d5f28" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186455378}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "dbfbb926-45f3-5b9a-aee3-a655234da83d" :question/math-academy-id "q-92829" :question/problem "Liam wants to paint a fence. He knows he needs $2$ liters of paint for $32$ square meters of fence. He creates a ratio table to determine the ratio of the volume of paint to the fenced area for different quantities.\n\n| Fence area (square meters) | Paint (liters) |\n| --- | --- |\n| $32$ | $2$ |\n| $80$ | $?$ |\n| $160$ | $10$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nWhat volume of paint does Liam need to paint $80$ square meters of the fence?" :question/worked-solution "We start with the ratio $32:2$ and write it as a fraction:\n\n$$\n\\frac{32}{2}\n$$\n\nNow we divide the numerator and the denominator by $2$ to find an equivalent ratio:\n\n$$\n\\frac{32÷2}{2÷2}=\\frac{16}{1}\n$$\n\nSo the numerator represents the area of the fence in ${\\text{m}}^{2}$ ($16$), and the denominator represents the volume of paint in liters ($1$).\n\nWe can make a numerator of $80$ by multiplying the numerator and denominator by $5$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{16\\times 5}{1\\times 5} & =\\frac{80}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe add this to our ratio table:\n\n| Fence area (square meters) | Paint (liters) |\n| --- | --- |\n| $32$ | $2$ |\n| $80$ | $5$ |\n| $160$ | $10$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nSo, Liam needs $5$ liters of paint for $80$ square meters of the fence."}]}
